# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Mykola Fiantsev
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
#
# Formatting policy, Firmware Repository Bootstrap Specification v0.3 §12.1.
#
# The first block below is the specification verbatim. Nothing in it is a
# preference; changing any of those keys is a specification change.
---
Language: Cpp

BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 100
PointerAlignment: Left
DerivePointerAlignment: false
SortIncludes: CaseSensitive
AllowShortFunctionsOnASingleLine: Empty
BreakBeforeBraces: Attach

# --- Additions beyond §12.1 -------------------------------------------------
#
# §12.1 fixes the base style and eight keys. The keys below are the minimum
# needed to make that base reproduce the structure the codebase already has, so
# that introducing the formatter is a formatting change and not a rewrite.

# The project uses C++17 (accepted decision D4). Telling clang-format the
# standard keeps it from reformatting valid C++17 as though newer syntax were
# available.
Standard: c++17

# Include blocks are preserved, not regrouped. This restates the LLVM default
# rather than changing it, and is stated explicitly because the reason is
# load-bearing: regrouping would sort across the `#pragma GCC diagnostic` guards
# that exist specifically to contain ESP-IDF and LVGL headers, and moving an
# include out of its guard breaks the build rather than merely the layout.
#
# A pragma line terminates an include block, so guarded includes sort within
# their own guard. Verified across all 70 project sources: adding explicit
# IncludeCategories on top of this changes not one byte, so none are set.
IncludeBlocks: Preserve

# Comments are hand-wrapped throughout, at the same 100 columns. Reflowing them
# would rewrite nearly every explanatory block in the repository for no gain.
ReflowComments: false
